{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The nakedness of your son's daughter or your daughter's daughter.</b> And it did not mention 'the nakedness of your daughter,' for this is a fortiori (ק״ו), in the manner of 'do not seethe a kid' — Scripture did not explicitly forbid eating, because it is also derived by a fortiori: if seething is forbidden, all the more so eating. And there I explained why Scripture expressed it in the language of seething and did not say 'do not eat.' And since it did not mention 'your daughter,' our Rabbis of blessed memory derived it in tractate Yevamot from a gezerah shavah of הנה הנה, and thus they said: Rabbi Yitzḥak bar Abdimi said — הנה הנה is derived, זמה זמה is derived. It is written regarding 'your son's daughter and your daughter's daughter': ״כי ערותך הנה״, and it is written regarding the prohibition of 'a woman and her daughter, and her son's daughter and her daughter's daughter': ״שארה הנה זמה היא״. Just as there, where it explicitly states that her daughter is forbidden, so too here, by the same logic, his son's daughter and his daughter's daughter — it follows that his daughter is forbidden, for we learn it by a gezerah shavah of הנה הנה."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:26:25.797893766Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}